{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1178710-examples-of-mythology-in-the-modern-age","id":1178710,"title":"Examples of Mythology in the Modern Age","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T03:12:49-08:00","id":1178710,"title":"Examples of Mythology in the Modern Age","content":"Doesn't look like there's a general thread for how modern life has adapted to gods and monsters, or vice-versa. Do the Theoi all hog Hermes's wifi connection? Have some enterprising humans set up a stable to provide that much-needed extra care for eight-legged horses and kelpies? Do selkies use dry cleaners, and what do they do when the stains won't come out of their second skins? Describe it here.<br /> <br /> <b>Poker Night:</b><br /> The tricksters must have been incredibly friendly to each other when they first met. There are even more liars and thieves out there? They must have amassed so many fancy things! And they won't expect someone even more clever and handsome to exist, so let's take some of those new toys before they work it out!<br /> Obviously this phase will have worn off pretty quickly, but the standard trickster's pride won't let them quit while they were behind. Over time, they would have had to set up a weekly poker night to keep the con going.<br /> Once a week, Loki, Coyote, Set, Elegba and Sun Wukong (Ganesha has an open invitation but doesn't consider these nights to be to anybody's betterment) sit down with a couple of decks of cards and try to fleece each other for all they're worth. They always start with poker, but persuading the other players that they're actually playing another game is not against the rules. Playing a hand where every card is three aces is not against the rules. Bringing other people is fine (they all recognise that the best tricks require a partner, witting or otherwise). In fact, the only rule that seems to stay the same every week is that if you get caught before you pull off the trick, you lose.<br /> Much as they hate to admit it, the gods are all fairly evenly matched - one night's big winner almost invariably loses all the money and priceless relics the next week. Still, it's all in good fun, and gives each pantheon a chance to &quot;lose&quot; their most accursed items, or snaffle some of the best toys from the others. And most importantly from the other gods' point of view, it gives the tricksters something to focus on other than their own favourite relics (A fact that leads even the most insular gods to support this activity).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T14:43:45-08:00","id":1179316,"title":"","content":"The Divine Matriarch Tea Society, founded by Hera, Frigg and Isis in the 19th century, meeting the afternoon of every New Moon, unless it falls on Sunday. Then they have brunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T15:19:27-08:00","id":1179323,"title":"","content":"a godly football club??<br /> <br /> a bounch of very athletic gods made up a team of scions and make a tournament every *idk* years<br /> <br /> The blue howls coached by athena<br /> the red thunder coached by thor<br /> Etcetc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T15:54:02-08:00","id":1179328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1178710-examples-of-mythology-in-the-modern-age?p=1179316#post1179316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Divine Matriarch Tea Society, founded by Hera, Frigg and Isis in the 19th century, meeting the afternoon of every New Moon, unless it falls on Sunday. Then they have brunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amaterasu found out about the club and holed herself in a cave again because she wasn't invited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:23:14-08:00","id":1179335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1178710-examples-of-mythology-in-the-modern-age?p=1179328#post1179328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amaterasu found out about the club and holed herself in a cave again because she wasn't invited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was going to consider her one of the early members, but that's too funny not to be part of it. <br /> <br /> This time, she was lured out with tea cakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:35:46-08:00","id":1179340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1178710-examples-of-mythology-in-the-modern-age?p=1179335#post1179335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I was going to consider her one of the early members, but that's too funny not to be part of it.<br /> <br /> This time, she was lured out with tea cakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well clearly what happened was that she wasn't invited to the FIRST meeting, she ran off to have a cry, then the others set up a new tea party with little cakes in front of the cave and called out to Amaterasu that they had a spot for her.<br /> <br /> She's been a regular ever since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:54:46-08:00","id":1179351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1178710-exampl