e=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well clearly what happened was that she wasn't invited to the FIRST meeting, she ran off to have a cry, then the others set up a new tea party with little cakes in front of the cave and called out to Amaterasu that they had a spot for her.<br /> <br /> She's been a regular ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some real cute stuff right there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T18:34:37-08:00","id":1179388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Not Quite Yoda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1178710-examples-of-mythology-in-the-modern-age#post1178710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't look like there's a general thread for how modern life has adapted to gods and monsters, or vice-versa. Do the Theoi all hog Hermes's wifi connection? Have some enterprising humans set up a stable to provide that much-needed extra care for eight-legged horses and kelpies? Do selkies use dry cleaners, and what do they do when the stains won't come out of their second skins? Describe it here.<br /> <br /> <b>Poker Night:</b><br /> The tricksters must have been incredibly friendly to each other when they first met. There are even more liars and thieves out there? They must have amassed so many fancy things! And they won't expect someone even more clever and handsome to exist, so let's take some of those new toys before they work it out!<br /> Obviously this phase will have worn off pretty quickly, but the standard trickster's pride won't let them quit while they were behind. Over time, they would have had to set up a weekly poker night to keep the con going.<br /> Once a week, Loki, Coyote, Set, Elegba and Sun Wukong (Ganesha has an open invitation but doesn't consider these nights to be to anybody's betterment) sit down with a couple of decks of cards and try to fleece each other for all they're worth. They always start with poker, but persuading the other players that they're actually playing another game is not against the rules. Playing a hand where every card is three aces is not against the rules. Bringing other people is fine (they all recognise that the best tricks require a partner, witting or otherwise). In fact, the only rule that seems to stay the same every week is that if you get caught before you pull off the trick, you lose.<br /> Much as they hate to admit it, the gods are all fairly evenly matched - one night's big winner almost invariably loses all the money and priceless relics the next week. Still, it's all in good fun, and gives each pantheon a chance to &amp;quot;lose&amp;quot; their most accursed items, or snaffle some of the best toys from the others. And most importantly from the other gods' point of view, it gives the tricksters something to focus on other than their own favourite relics (A fact that leads even the most insular gods to support this activity).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This literally happens in every game I run where the Gods are present, regardless of system. I even had a short story published called &quot;Gods Playing Poker&quot; that focused on it. Poker Night is one of those things that just needs to show up. I'm glad I'm not the only one that thinks so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}